  "overview": "**Biings Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#8c50b9` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `Plush` with `Source Sans Pro` body copy (40px display down to 15px body), unified by `7px` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Biings**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (https://biings.design/#/color). Inventory: **72** colors, **7** typography steps, and **24** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 24 component tokens with documented paddings: `.25em .875em`, `1.65rem 1.75rem`, `1.625rem 1.75rem`, `.8em`, `8px 12px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f7efe9` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`inset 0 1px 2px rgba(19,10,26,.06)`, `inset 0 1px 2px rgba(19,10,26,.06)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#8c50b9` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#8c50b9` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.9:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Plush` headings with `Source Sans Pro` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `7px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (7px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f7efe9` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `7px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
